{title: Simple Gifts}
{artist: Joseph Brackett, 1848}
{key: D}
{tempo: 100}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, hymn}

[D]'Tis the gift to be simple, 'tis the gift to be [A]free
'Tis the gift to come down where we [A7]ought to [D]be
And when we find ourselves in the place just [A]right
'Twill be in the valley of [A7]love and de[D]light

{start_of_chorus}
When true sim[D]plicity is [A]gained
To bow and to bend we shan't be a[D]shamed
To turn, turn will [A]be our de[D]light
Till by turning, turning we [A]come round [D]right
